1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,020
The best engineering teams don't ship faster because they type faster.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,080
They ship on a platform.

3
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:10,440
Years of discipline, that most teams never get to build.

4
00:00:11,190 --> 00:00:13,490
orun turns that discipline into intent.

5
00:00:13,810 --> 00:00:14,510
What exists.

6
00:00:14,690 --> 00:00:15,530
Where it ships.

7
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:17,190
And the rules it lives by.

8
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:20,910
One open-source binary compiles it into a single plan.

9
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:23,250
Same inputs, same plan.

10
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,130
Every time.

11
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,000
Policy runs at compile time.

12
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:30,380
So when an agent breaks a rule, it fails in the plan.

13
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:31,560
Not in production.

14
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:33,710
Want the whole platform?

15
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:34,670
Pick a baseline.

16
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:35,830
Connect your cloud.

17
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:37,820
About an hour later:

18
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:41,680
forty-four components, twelve bounded contexts, three environments.

19
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,380
Live, in your repo.

20
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:46,100
Then every commit converges.

21
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:47,480
Forty-one jobs.

22
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,160
All green.

23
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:50,120
orun.

24
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:51,700
Platform discipline, compiled.

25
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:52,720
Open source.
